# state: any   (golden 9153c63300da, the same as gta-3.route)
# Grand Theft Auto III (5454000E): a DRIVING route (lane.gta3drive1017, #433).
# NOT PROVEN until a run's frames show the car moving: frames minutes apart at
# different places, radar turning. gta-3.route is the on-foot measurement and
# stays as it is.
#
# Boot: copied verbatim from gta-3.route up to its `waitfor fist-hud` (see
# that file's header for why there is no START).
#
# Entry gate: the scene itself, Claude on foot beside the Kuruma on the
# bridge ramp (refs/gta-3-drive/at-kuruma.png, the car and the wall behind
# it, cut from 1-1792280173-...-1364097 164333-pregameplay.png at
# 830,440,450,220). Three of five runs reach exactly this frame by
# `pregameplay` (1364097, 1364296, and the Playable run
# 1-1791792686-lane.local-32437) and stand in it until input moves them
# (1364097: unchanged from 16:43:33 to 16:50:00). tools/route_gate.py: 0.00,
# 0.25, 0.37-0.67 on those frames; 19.87 and up on the 31 others (cutscenes,
# the in-car frames, the drives). Threshold 10.
#
# Two gates before this one failed:
# - fist-hud (gta-3.route's) matched at once in both pilots
#   (1-1792275531-...-343857, 1-1792275540-...-346093), whose A-train ended
#   with Claude already in a car in Red Light District / Chinatown at a 05:xx
#   clock (153645-pregameplay.png, 154630-pregameplay.png); the Y press
#   there exited the car. The weapon icon is up on every in-game screen.
# - the tutorial box "Enter or exit a vehicle: Y" (enter-help.png) never
#   showed after `pregameplay` in either run of the first drive pair: it is
#   up only in the first seconds of the mission, which the A-train covers.
#   Both runs timed out on it, standing beside the car.
# A run whose A-train ends anywhere else times out here and is void.
#
# Entry: press Y until the scene changes (press-until's reference is the
# state before the press works). The game takes the nearest upright car
# within 10 units (re3 CPlayerInfo::FindClosestCarSectorList,
# `dist <= 10.0f`), so one Y walks Claude to the door and in, and the camera
# swings behind the car; up to 3 presses 5 s apart cover a press the host's
# adb drops (both pilots logged vsock accept timeouts). The 6 s after it
# covers the camera swing and the "Accelerate" box. 8-Ball is already in the
# passenger seat by then: 1-1792282254-...-1563459's onfoot frame (clock
# 05:12) shows him in it before the Y press.
#
# Warm-up, before `mark gameplay`: the scored loop's cycle six times (~70 s),
# with three frames a cycle (mid-throttle, after the Y, after the reverse).
# In 1563459 the gate and the entry worked (matched at 0 s, in after one Y),
# but the mission restarted within ~30 s of the throttle (clock 05:25 in the
# car at 17:14:12, 04:18 on foot beside the Kuruma at 17:14:46), and no frame
# covered those 30 s. These frames do, and they are outside the scored
# window, so their screencaps cost the measurement nothing. `mark gameplay`
# comes after them, so the scored window starts in a car that has been
# moving.
#
# Driving: RT accelerates (pad.sh: the triggers are not swapped; 0..32767),
# LT brakes and reverses, LX steers (-32767..32767; the Nova and the Thor
# cache the same ranges). Never START or BACK.
#
# Why this shape: three tries flipped the Kuruma on the bridge ramp, and a
# flip fails the mission ("You flipped your wheels!") and restarts it with
# Claude on foot beside the car (NOTES.md 8.3-8.5).
# - 1-1792283158-...-1853100: full throttle, 0.6 s full-lock pulses. On the
#   first left pulse the car hit a lamp post on the ramp's wall and landed on
#   its roof (172943-warm.png, clock 05:51).
# - 1-1792283746-...-2035473: RT 22000 and a third of lock for 0.8 s. The same
#   lamp post, the same flip, ~5 s into the throttle (174033-warm.png, 05:42).
#   The ramp is narrow and its lamp posts stand on the walls, so any steering
#   at speed there reaches one within 2 s.
# So:
# - No steering going forward. The car runs straight, and turns only while
#   reversing, slowly. Each cycle: RT 18000 for 6 s, brake straight for 2 s,
#   then reverse 1.5 s with the wheel turned. Two turns one way, one the
#   other, so the heading walks rather than oscillates.
# - A Y at the end of each throttle stretch. GTA III, unlike Vice City, lets
#   the player leave a car only at low speed or at a stop (Grand Theft Wiki,
#   "Bail Out"), so at speed the press does nothing. After a restart it walks
#   Claude back into the Kuruma (8-Ball waits in it, 8.3), which the old loop
#   could not do. A car stuck against a wall is slow, so there Y gets out,
#   and the next cycle's Y gets back in.
# - A frame every cycle (~11 s), so a restart or a wreck in the scored window
#   shows in the frames and goes to drive_judge.py's --exclude.
#
wait 55
repeat 4 {
    press A 300
    wait 5
}
shot introskip
repeat 12 {
    press A 300
    wait 5
}
shot pregameplay
waitfor at-kuruma 240 830,440,450,220 10
shot onfoot
press-until Y at-kuruma 3 5 830,440,450,220 10
wait 6
shot incar
repeat 2 {
    axis RT 18000
    wait 3
    shot warm
    wait 3
    press Y 300
    shot warmy
    axis RT min
    axis LT max
    wait 2
    axis LX max
    wait 1.5
    axis LT min
    axis LX mid
    shot warmr
    axis RT 18000
    wait 3
    shot warm
    wait 3
    press Y 300
    shot warmy
    axis RT min
    axis LT max
    wait 2
    axis LX max
    wait 1.5
    axis LT min
    axis LX mid
    shot warmr
    axis RT 18000
    wait 3
    shot warm
    wait 3
    press Y 300
    shot warmy
    axis RT min
    axis LT max
    wait 2
    axis LX min
    wait 1.5
    axis LT min
    axis LX mid
    shot warmr
}
mark gameplay
repeat forever {
    axis RT 18000
    wait 6
    press Y 300
    shot drive
    axis RT min
    axis LT max
    wait 2
    axis LX max
    wait 1.5
    axis LT min
    axis LX mid
    axis RT 18000
    wait 6
    press Y 300
    shot drive
    axis RT min
    axis LT max
    wait 2
    axis LX max
    wait 1.5
    axis LT min
    axis LX mid
    axis RT 18000
    wait 6
    press Y 300
    shot drive
    axis RT min
    axis LT max
    wait 2
    axis LX min
    wait 1.5
    axis LT min
    axis LX mid
}
